{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nDuring execution-phase plan review, batched overlap-judge calls took 216–311 seconds and returned oversized malformed JSON with runaway candidate_id content. The final catch safely abstained, but only after multiple long generations. Phase 1 proved the overlap call inherits generic 16,000-token, three-structured-attempt, four-transport-attempt, and 600-second-per-request budgets; it declares no overlap-local limits. The original 9022 story and ADR 0086 require a bounded advisory classifier whose timeout/error/malformed output degrades promptly to abstention.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\n`judge_batch` builds a native structured `RunRequest` without operation-local output, structured-retry, transport-retry, or timeout bounds. Generic runner policy therefore permits three full structured generations and transport retries before the advisory catch executes. A token cap alone still retried three times; schema validation alone acted only after the oversized payload existed. The durable runtime proof is recorded in the Phase 1 RCA comment.\n\n## Repair plan\n\n- Extend the internal `RunRequest` budget contract with lowering-only per-request seams for structured-output retries, transport attempts, and request timeout, preserving current defaults for every existing caller. Keep `output_token_limit` as the existing lowering-only output seam.\n- Apply those seams in the effective runner configuration and both native/prompted structured-output paths so an injected/shared runner and every provider path honor the same request-local limits.\n- Give overlap judge calls explicit advisory budgets: 1,024 output tokens (the c403 live valid six-candidate response used 599), one structured attempt, one transport attempt, and a 60-second request timeout. Any bound hit continues through the existing logged safe-abstention path.\n- Preserve valid verdict demultiplexing and aggregation behavior byte-for-byte outside budget metadata.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit/contract tier through the real `judge_batch` → `PydanticAIRunner` structured path with a deterministic FunctionModel. Prove the fixture reaches malformed runaway output, the current path is RED by making three attempts/inheriting 16K, and the repaired path makes one bounded attempt then returns exact all-candidate abstention.\n- Settings-seam tests prove request-local retry/timeout values can only lower global policy and that callers omitting them retain current settings.\n- Negative control: a valid six-candidate verdict under the bounded request retains label-keyed mapping and relation behavior.\n- Mutation: remove the overlap-local limits and confirm the held-out oracle returns RED.\n- Original-path replication: run an overlap-enabled plan-review scenario and confirm malformed/truncated output abstains within the declared bound without blocking or fabricating overlap.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A runaway overlap response is capped at 1,024 output tokens; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py -k runaway`.\n- [ ] A malformed overlap response makes one structured generation; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py -k runaway`.\n- [ ] A failed overlap request makes one transport attempt; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py -k transport_attempt`.\n- [ ] An overlap request carries a 60-second request timeout; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py -k request_budget`.\n- [ ] Timeout, truncation, and malformed output each return exact all-candidate abstention; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py -k bounded_abstention`.\n- [ ] Valid batched verdicts retain label-keyed mapping and aggregation; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py`.\n- [ ] Callers omitting request-local limits retain existing policy; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py tests/unit/test_runner_hardening.py`.\n- [ ] The held-out oracle returns RED when the overlap-local limits are removed; checked by the recorded mutation run.\n- [ ] Focused tests, `make lint`, and `make typecheck` exit 0.\n- [ ] An overlap-enabled original-path replication abstains within the declared bound and returns no fabricated overlap finding; checked by the recorded live run."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786252657425344001,"uuid":"3df93130-5cde-4cf7-af45-958904bdf939"}